# Code owners for the approval-bearing paths. Branch protection on `main`
# requires a review from a code owner before a pull request touching any of
# these paths can merge — that requirement, not the CI check, is what makes an
# unreviewed approval unmergeable.

# The approval records themselves.
/.sigildex/approvals/**       @sigildex/skill-approvers

# The workflow that checks them. Under `pull_request`, GitHub runs the workflow
# file as the pull request writes it, so editing the workflow is as
# approval-affecting as editing a record.
/.github/workflows/**         @sigildex/skill-approvers

# This file, so the owner set cannot be edited out from under itself.
/.github/CODEOWNERS           @sigildex/skill-approvers

# The active skills directory. The workflow watches ONE skill/record pair, so a
# pull request that adds a new skill directory with no approval record touches
# nothing the workflow checks — covering the directory here is what makes that
# pull request need a code-owner review.
/.claude/skills/**            @sigildex/skill-approvers

# Pre-publication only: the vendored tool tarball. Its digest is pinned in the
# workflow, so swapping it fails the check; ownership here is belt-and-braces.
/vendor/**                    @sigildex/skill-approvers
